            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Wait, what?\n\nThis doesn't \"deprecate\", it \"removes\", right?\n\nWe have all these upstream systems relying on this support.  Who is going to modernize them?\n\n```\n$ find -name \"*.yaml\" | grep -i led-manager\n./meta-ibm/meta-palmetto/recipes-phosphor/leds/palmetto-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-ibm/meta-romulus/recipes-phosphor/leds/romulus-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-ibm/recipes-phosphor/leds/swift-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-ibm/meta-genesis3/recipes-phosphor/leds/gen3-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-ibm/meta-sbp1/recipes-phosphor/leds/sbp1-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-facebook/meta-bletchley/recipes-phosphor/leds/bletchley-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-facebook/meta-yosemite4/recipes-phosphor/leds/yosemite4-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-inventec/meta-starscream/recipes-phosphor/leds/starscream-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-nuvoton/meta-evb-npcm845/recipes-phosphor/leds/evb-npcm845-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-quanta/meta-olympus-nuvoton/recipes-phosphor/leds/olympus-nuvoton-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-quanta/meta-gbs/recipes-phosphor/leds/gbs-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-yadro/meta-nicole/recipes-phosphor/leds/nicole-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-yadro/meta-vegman/recipes-phosphor/leds/rx20-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-yadro/meta-vegman/recipes-phosphor/leds/vegman-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-amd/meta-ethanolx/recipes-phosphor/leds/ethanolx-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-amd/meta-daytonax/recipes-phosphor/leds/daytonax-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-fii/meta-mori/recipes-phosphor/leds/mori-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-intel-openbmc/meta-common/recipes-phosphor/leds/intel-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n./meta-ufispace/meta-ncplite/recipes-phosphor/leds/ncplite-led-manager-config/led.yaml\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "yes, i should change the wording there :)\n\n\nI was not expecting this to be merged right away, i just wanted to get some general feedback from the people involved. \n\nLike Patrick Rudolph and Andrew. \n\nIf people are ok with the idea and do not have \nsome requirement that\nthey must configure at compile time,\n\nthen i can take the time to create\n some small script to migrate the upstream configs.\n \n \nSince i do not have that history,\ndo you know by chance which configuratiom format came first?\n\nOr why a second configuration format was introduced?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "pushed the corresponding change in openbmc/openbmc gerrit\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc/+/78131\n\nhappy to receive any feedback on that \ud83d\ude0a"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Changed the wording to clarify that the patch indeed removes the yaml configuration option.\n\n> We have all these upstream systems relying on this support. Who is going to modernize them?\n\nAdded a link to the corresponding change in openbmc/openbmc which migrates the configurations."
                }
            ],
